MV

Purpose

MV (Medium Voltage) is the second electrical technology tier.

The player transitions from basic electrical industry to more advanced and scalable industrial systems.

MV introduces higher-capacity power infrastructure, more complex processing chains, improved machinery, and larger-scale automation.

The player should begin operating a true industrial facility capable of supporting multiple production lines simultaneously.

Resources

MV primarily uses:

Iron
Copper
Tin
Steel
Aluminium
Lead
Silver
Gold
Redstone
Rubber
Other materials required for medium-voltage infrastructure

Higher-tier materials remain restricted until their respective technological stages.

Tools

MV introduces improved industrial tools and equipment.

These tools should provide greater efficiency than LV equipment while remaining limited to capabilities appropriate for the MV tier.

Tools should support large-scale industrial construction and resource gathering without replacing higher-tier equipment.

Processing

MV introduces more advanced multi-stage processing.

Production chains should increasingly require:

Raw material processing
Material refinement
Intermediate components
Advanced components
Machine components
Electrical components

Processing should become more efficient than LV while also becoming more complex.

The player should increasingly rely on automated production chains rather than manual crafting.

Machines

MV introduces advanced electrical machinery capable of significantly greater throughput than LV machines.

Machines should provide:

Advanced material processing
Higher-efficiency ore processing
Advanced component manufacturing
Industrial chemical processing
Large-scale resource processing
Higher-throughput automation

MV machines should require substantially greater infrastructure and power capacity than LV machines.

Higher-tier machines remain locked.

Power

Medium Voltage becomes the primary industrial power infrastructure.

The player must expand their electrical system to support:

Higher power generation
Higher machine throughput
Larger electrical networks
Industrial power distribution
Power storage
Multiple simultaneous production lines

Power generation should become a significant infrastructure project.

The player should need to plan electrical capacity rather than simply placing additional generators whenever more power is required.

Automation

MV greatly expands industrial automation.

The player should be able to operate:

Large automated production lines
Multi-stage processing chains
Automated component manufacturing
Automated chemical processing
Large material transportation systems
Automated resource buffering
Parallel machine arrays

Automation should increasingly become necessary rather than optional.

The complexity of MV production should make manual crafting impractical for large quantities.

Create Integration

Create continues to provide mechanical and logistical infrastructure.

Create should primarily be used for:

Factory logistics
Mechanical transportation
Material handling
Mechanical automation
Specialized mechanical processing

Create may interact with MV systems, but must not bypass MV technological requirements.

GregTech Integration

GregTech remains the primary technological progression system.

MV introduces more advanced GregTech machinery, materials, and processing chains.

GregTech progression should require increasingly complex infrastructure and multi-stage production.

The player should begin preparing the materials and machinery required for HV.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides additional MV machinery and processing systems.

Its machines should be integrated into the same technological progression and contribute to specialized or complementary production chains.

Modern Industrialization must not provide an independent progression path that bypasses MV requirements.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism becomes increasingly useful during MV.

Its machines may provide advanced processing and specialized industrial capabilities, but their progression must remain synchronized with the pack's technological tiers.

Mekanism must not provide unrestricted access to processing or power capabilities belonging to higher tiers.

Requirements

The player must complete LV before entering MV.

The player should have:

Established reliable LV electrical infrastructure
Automated essential LV production chains
Produced the components required for MV machinery
Established access to MV-tier materials
Built sufficient electrical capacity for MV machinery
Established automated production of essential industrial components

Exit Condition

MV ends when the player has established a large-scale electrical industry capable of supporting the substantially greater complexity of HV.

The player must:

Establish reliable MV power infrastructure
Automate essential MV production chains
Produce the components required for HV machinery
Complete the required MV processing chains
Establish the infrastructure necessary for higher-voltage production

Completion of these requirements unlocks HV.

The MV stage should leave the player with a mature industrial facility capable of operating multiple complex production chains simultaneously.
